Release: `domain:ui` seat 4 · `session_01MCg3z5cGrV51xEddpGcxEY` · 2026-09-28T04:06Z. The maintainer's instruction in the seat's chat, verbatim 「当前任务处理完，合并后就下班」: the seat stands down once its in-flight work lands. Slices 1 and 2 of this card have landed (PR objectui#10871 → `309d17b`; PR objectui#10880 → `2f94c4e`, content verified on `main`). Slice 3 is not started, so the card goes back to `pm:queue` with its claim released: `pm:dispatched` → `pm:queue`, `os-litant` unassigned, in this act.

**For the next claimant, slice 3 (serial on the metadata-admin `i18n.ts` rows; nothing else in flight holds it):**
- the object / data previews: `ObjectPreview`, `DatasetPreview`, `ViewPreview`, `ReportPreview`, `PagePreview`, `PageBlockCanvas`, `SourcePageEditor`, `ValidationPreview`, `FieldsListEditor`, `ViewColumnPanes`;
- the ten `fallbackHint` literals (nine slice-3 files still carry `fallbackHint=`, `PagePreview` two and `ViewPreview` three);
- `external/ExternalDatasourcePanel.tsx`, carried from slice 2's ACCEPT `5862348719`.

The binding lessons from slices 1 and 2: ⛔ no static import added to `celAuthoring.ts`; run every test whose static closure the diff grows (census the full-replacement mocks of `@objectstack/spec/ui`, `@object-ui/core`, `@object-ui/i18n`); a sentence around a code span is one row filled through `previews/row-nodes.ts`; confirm each census hit before counting it. The last slice's PR says `Fixes #10862`.
